    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0687" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/11–1248</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Permanent Representative to the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tsiang</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="54" xml:id="d580-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-12">November 12, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Under instructions from Dr.
                    Wang Shih-chieh, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, I am transmitting to you an
                        <pb facs="0688" n="678" xml:id="pg678"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>, setting forth certain considerations
                    relating to the American aid program in China and our common relations with
                    Japan.</p>
                <p>Dr. Wang further instructed me to say that he drafted the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> after his talks with you<anchor n="55" xml:id="d580-f2"/>
                    and Mr. Hoffman in Paris.</p>
                <p>With warm regards,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tingfu</hi> F. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Tsiang</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d580-a1.xml" xpointer="d580-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="54" type="source" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Handed to the Secretary of State by Dr. Tsiang on November 13; the Secretary of
                    State was in Paris on official mission.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d580-f2" n="55" xml:id="d580-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning these conversations, see <ref target="#pg192">pp.
                        192</ref> ff., <hi rendition="#italic">passim.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
